<title>ITALY: Italy's Trieste sees May CPI at 0.3 pct mo/mo.</title>
<headline>Italy's Trieste sees May CPI at 0.3 pct mo/mo.</headline>
<dateline>TRIESTE, Italy 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Trieste said its May consumer price index stood at 0.3 percent month on month and 1.1 percent year on year.</p>
<p>In April, Trieste's inflation rate was -0.6 percent month on month and 1.2 percent year on year.</p>
<p>Trieste is one of 11 Italian cities publishing inflation data on Tuesday and Wednesday. The city's CPI has a weighting of 2.49 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>The following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to April 1997):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		     0.3   (-0.6)    1.1    (1.2)</p>
<p>    Food				  0.1   (-0.4)    0.3    (1.1)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.4    (0.6)    3.1    (2.8)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges  -0.2    (0.2)    2.9    (3.2)</p>
<p>    Furniture			   0.6    (0.0)    2.3    (2.8)</p>
<p>    Health services		   0.0    (0.0)    1.8    (1.9)</p>
<p>    Transportation		    0.2   (-4.8)   -2.5   (-2.3)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture     0.4    (0.0)   -0.4   (-0.7)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.0    (0.0)    4.8    (4.8)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.0    (0.0)    2.9    (3.0)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 1.4    (0.1)    0.7   (-0.7)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129507</p>
